Title: 0009-free-sprite-lists
Repository: micropoliscore
Base-Commit: 69ccf87ed72d2d2950b70cf16ef1391439bd9d48
Requires: 0008-scenario-load-errors.patch
Author: aros-micropolis project
Date: 2026-09-20
Upstream-Status: candidate
Scope: generic native engine lifetime; no gameplay behavior change

Problem:
  Micropolis::destroy() released map arrays but retained every active and pooled SimSprite. Repeated startup previews therefore accumulated native heap objects and their std::string members.
Solution:
  Delete both disjoint sprite ownership lists, clear their global aliases, then release map arrays. A host allocation-tracking regression covers active and pooled objects under ASan/UBSan.
Validation:
  Host clang C++17, ASan/UBSan: tests/engine-lifetime/run-tests.sh tracks
  allocations made by newSprite() and verifies that destroying a city releases
  both active and pooled objects (1/1, 2026-09-20). Existing real-engine suites:
  startup 60/60, disasters/scenarios 125/125, budget 0 failures, simulation
  14/14 plus timer 13/13, sprite renderer 16/16. Full nine-patch isolated
  reproduction passes. Complete game compiles and links for AROS One ABIv11
  and mainline v1; no guest runtime was needed or claimed for this ownership fix.
Removal:
  Permanent ownership fix; remove only if upstream adopts equivalent cleanup.

diff --git a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
index e0024b2..55d1e49 100644
--- a/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
+++ b/packages/micropolis-engine/src/micropolis.cpp
@@ -704,9 +704,24 @@ void Micropolis::init()
 void Micropolis::destroy()
 {
 
+    // Active sprites and the reuse pool are disjoint lists of objects made
+    // with new SimSprite().  They own std::string members, so release them
+    // with delete rather than the engine's raw-memory helpers.
+    while (spriteList != NULL) {
+        SimSprite *sprite = spriteList;
+        spriteList = sprite->next;
+        delete sprite;
+    }
+    while (freeSprites != NULL) {
+        SimSprite *sprite = freeSprites;
+        freeSprites = sprite->next;
+        delete sprite;
+    }
+    memset(globalSprites, 0, sizeof(SimSprite *) * SPRITE_COUNT);
+
     destroyMapArrays();
 
-    // TODO: Clean up all other stuff:
+    // TODO: Clean up other engine-owned resources.
 
 }
 
